div><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/nyc/">New York</a> / Parking and property-use signs</p><p class="eyebrow">VISION GRAPHICS · NEW YORK</p><h1>Parking and property-use signs</h1><p class="lead">Parking signs help a property explain where vehicles should go and which spaces have a particular purpose. They need clear wording, a sensible location and a format that suits the viewing distance. For New York property managers, Vision Graphics can help organize a consistent set of on-site messages, from visitor parking identification to delivery instructions. The property team should supply approved wording and confirm placement authority. A printed sign alone does not establish a legal restriction or authorize changes to public streets.</p><p class="review-note">Planning guide · </p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/nyc/contact/?product=Parking%20and%20property-use%20signs">Discuss your project <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="#options">Explore options <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div><figure class="project-image product-photo"><img src="/nyc/assets/vg-wayfinding-ada-960.webp" srcset="/nyc/assets/vg-wayfinding-ada-480.webp 480w, /nyc/assets/vg-wayfinding-ada-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Signage example related to Parking and property-use signs" loading="lazy"><figcaption>VG portfolio example</figcaption></figure></section><section class="wrap section article-layout"><article><section><h2>Make the instruction specific</h2><p>Separate the destination from any conditions of use. Avoid cramming several exceptions into a small panel; a simple hierarchy makes the most important instruction easier to see. Keep terminology consistent across entrances, parking areas and delivery points.</p></section><section><h2>Confirm placement and wording</h2><p>List each sign location and photograph the approach. Identify who owns or controls the surface and whether the sign relates to private property or a public area. Review approved language and any required symbols with the responsible property or legal professional before production.</p></section><section id="options"><p class="eyebrow">MATERIALS &amp; APPROACHES</p><h2>Find the right fit.</h2><div class="options-grid"><div><h3>Space identification</h3><p>Label visitor, staff or assigned spaces with an organized numbering system.</p></div><div><h3>Delivery and access directions</h3><p>Guide authorized vehicles to the appropriate on-site destination.</p></div><div><h3>Property instruction panels</h3><p>Present approved conditions in a clear, readable layout.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Where it can work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Private parking areas</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Managed commercial properties</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Loading and service areas</li></ul></section><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Can you supply enforceable restriction wording?<span>+</span></summary><p>The property owner and appropriate professional should approve legal wording and authority. This page does not provide legal advice.</p></details><details><summary>Can signs be installed on public posts?<span>+</span></summary><p>Public placement requires the relevant authorization. Confirm the approved location and responsible party before planning attachment.</p></details></section></article><aside class="product-aside"><p class="eyebrow">LET’S START WITH THE DETAILS</p><h3>Have a space in mind?</h3><p>A photo, a few measurements and your project ZIP help us ask the right questions.</p><a href="/nyc/contact/?photo=1" class="btn dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-camera" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.997 4a2 2 0 0 1 1.76 1.05l.486.9A2 2 0 0 0 18.003 7H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V9a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h1.997a2 2 0 0 0 1.759-1.048l.489-.904A2 2 0 0 1 10.004 4z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle></svg> Send a project photo</a><hr><h3>Related possibilities</h3><a href="/nyc/directional-signs/">Directional signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/real-estate-signs/">Real estate signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" s